    <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
      <body>
        <div rend="parallel">
            <p xml:id="Aink450-kilavi">vēntaṟku uṟṟuḻip pirinta talaimakaṉ viṉaimuṟṟāmaiyiṉ pācaṟaikkaṇ iruntu taṉ maṉakkaruttu uraittatu.</p>
            <p xml:lang="en">The hero, who had separated for a royal emergency, staying in the warcamp because the work was incomplete, spoke as his minds intent.<note xml:lang="en" place="foot">In other words, his inner thought, or something similar.</note></p>
              </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
          <lg xml:id="Aink450">        
            <l>muracumā ṟiraṭṭu maruntoḻiṟ pakaitaṇintu</l>
            <l>nāṭumuṉ ṉiyarō pīṭukeḻu vēntaṉ</l>
            <l>veyya vuyirkkunōy taṇiyac</l>
            <l>ceyyō ḷiḷamulaip paṭīiyareṉ kaṇṇē.</l>
        </lg>  
 <lg xml:lang="en">                    
<l>The enmity of the difficult task where drums resound in turn<note xml:lang="en" place="foot">The idea being that the dums of the hero's army and that of the enemy's beat one after the other.</note> having subsided,</l>
<l>may the king abounding in greatness consider his land.<note xml:lang="en" place="foot">I understand this as an euphemism for planning to return home.</note></l>
<l>So that the affliction that makes [her] sigh hotly subsides,</l>
<l>may the my eyes fall upon the young breasts of the perfect one.</l> 
</lg>                      
        </div>
      </body>
